cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use UNIFORM in your academic research, game-theoretic verification, or formal theorem proving, please cite it as follows."
title: "UNIFORM: Exact Rational and Real-Algebraic Framework for Multiplayer Quitting and Stochastic Games"
abstract: >-
  UNIFORM is an exact-arithmetic computational research workbench and formal verification
  suite designed to investigate the existence of uniform equilibrium in finite multiplayer
  quitting games and small stochastic games. The system eliminates numerical float artifacts
  through exact rational arithmetic and algebraic field arithmetic with Sturm root isolation.
  It provides a high-throughput deterministic Rust scanner (43.9M games/s), multi-solver
  SMT-CAD artifact generators (Z3/cvc5), exact Sylvester resultant elimination engines,
  and machine-checked Lean 4 Mathlib proofs with zero axioms and zero proof debt.
